{"reference":"Genesis 22","book":"Genesis","chapter":22,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Deeds and faith","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"James pairs Abraham and Rahab as examples in which deeds enact or complete faith. Applied to Genesis 22, that is a disputed reception-history connection: it identifies how a later writer reads Abraham's action without reducing the chapter to that later formulation alone.","verse_refs":["Genesis 22:1-19"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_022_636c9593bc4c97461c1e180d"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
